1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,421
March 17, 2015.

2
00:00:02,421 --> 00:00:04,410
The Los Angeles area.

3
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:08,104
A line of officers moves along a fence.

4
00:00:08,554 --> 00:00:10,129
On their vests: Police.

5
00:00:10,129 --> 00:00:13,141
Homeland Security Investigations. Gang Unit.

6
00:00:13,591 --> 00:00:16,170
This is one address, in one city.

7
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:19,609
Over six weeks, scenes like this play out in

8
00:00:19,609 --> 00:00:22,423
282 cities across the United States.

9
00:00:22,873 --> 00:00:27,503
ICE says 976 gang members and associates were

10
00:00:27,503 --> 00:00:28,429
arrested.

11
00:00:28,429 --> 00:00:31,001
From 239 different gangs.

12
00:00:31,451 --> 00:00:33,813
It was called Project Wildfire.

13
00:00:33,813 --> 00:00:36,405
How do you hit 282 cities at once?

14
00:00:36,405 --> 00:00:39,301
And who actually ends up in handcuffs?

15
00:00:39,901 --> 00:00:42,781
This is the case of the national gang surge.

16
00:00:45,381 --> 00:00:48,150
To understand Wildfire, start with the unit

17
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:48,923
that ran it.

18
00:00:49,373 --> 00:00:53,221
Homeland Security Investigations, HSI, is part

19
00:00:53,221 --> 00:00:54,225
of ICE, U.S.

20
00:00:54,225 --> 00:00:57,237
Immigration and Customs Enforcement.

21
00:00:57,237 --> 00:01:00,082
It has its own National Gang Unit.

22
00:01:00,532 --> 00:01:03,860
In its 2017 surge, ICE said the targets were

23
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:07,491
gang members tied to crime that crosses borders.

24
00:01:07,491 --> 00:01:08,776
Drug trafficking.

25
00:01:08,776 --> 00:01:10,138
Weapons smuggling.

26
00:01:10,138 --> 00:01:12,861
Human smuggling and sex trafficking.

27
00:01:12,861 --> 00:01:14,676
Murder and racketeering.

28
00:01:15,126 --> 00:01:18,587
Since February 2005, that work has run under

29
00:01:18,587 --> 00:01:19,530
one program.

30
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:21,654
Operation Community Shield.

31
00:01:22,104 --> 00:01:27,494
By ICE's own count, the program passed 30,000

32
00:01:27,494 --> 00:01:30,009
gang arrests by 2013.

33
00:01:30,009 --> 00:01:31,806
36,000 by 2015.

34
00:01:31,806 --> 00:01:33,603
47,000 by 2017.

35
00:01:34,053 --> 00:01:37,773
And its most visible tool is the surge. A few weeks.

36
00:01:37,773 --> 00:01:40,134
Field offices across the country.

37
00:01:40,134 --> 00:01:42,567
Local, state and federal partners.

38
00:01:42,567 --> 00:01:44,570
All moving at the same time.

39
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,748
Summer, 2013.

40
00:01:47,198 --> 00:01:50,964
From July 15 to August 9, HSI ran a surge

41
00:01:50,964 --> 00:01:53,535
called Project Razor's Edge.

42
00:01:53,535 --> 00:01:55,923
Its main target was MS-13.

43
00:01:56,373 --> 00:02:00,084
25 HSI field offices took part, working with

44
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:03,627
local, state, tribal and federal agencies.

45
00:02:04,077 --> 00:02:07,293
The field offices and their partners worked up

46
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:10,369
threat assessments, focused on MS-13 members

47
00:02:10,369 --> 00:02:13,516
with prior convictions, foreign-born members,

48
00:02:13,516 --> 00:02:14,914
and those on parole.

49
00:02:15,364 --> 00:02:18,400
In Maryland, teams fanned out from a parking

50
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,953
lot staging area, vehicle by vehicle.

51
00:02:21,403 --> 00:02:25,329
When it ended, HSI reported 361 arrests.

52
00:02:25,329 --> 00:02:29,745
263 of them were gang members and associates.

53
00:02:30,195 --> 00:02:33,757
They came from 43 gangs, in 71 cities.

54
00:02:34,207 --> 00:02:38,280
158 of those arrested were MS-13 members and

55
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,298
associates.

56
00:02:39,298 --> 00:02:41,149
4 were gang leaders.

57
00:02:41,149 --> 00:02:45,407
202 were foreign nationals, from 15 countries.

58
00:02:45,857 --> 00:02:48,900
The charges ranged from illegal re-entry and

59
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,666
aggravated robbery to kidnapping, sexual

60
00:02:51,666 --> 00:02:53,879
assault and first-degree murder.

61
00:02:54,329 --> 00:02:57,896
In Petersburg, Virginia, a 19-year-old MS-13

62
00:02:57,896 --> 00:03:01,057
member from El Salvador was arrested on

63
00:03:01,057 --> 00:03:05,273
charges of first-degree murder and illegal re-entry.

64
00:03:05,723 --> 00:03:08,825
In New Mexico, an MS-13 member and two

65
00:03:08,825 --> 00:03:12,581
associates were arrested on stolen-firearm and

66
00:03:12,581 --> 00:03:13,805
heroin charges.

67
00:03:13,805 --> 00:03:16,826
Agents also seized 5 stolen handguns.

68
00:03:16,826 --> 00:03:20,827
At the time, these were charges, not convictions.

69
00:03:21,277 --> 00:03:25,683
Agents also seized 28 firearms, and about 770

70
00:03:25,683 --> 00:03:27,250
grams of heroin.

71
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:30,694
In Dallas, the same routine. Vests. Stairs.

72
00:03:30,694 --> 00:03:31,391
Handcuffs.

73
00:03:31,841 --> 00:03:33,236
263 gang arrests.

74
00:03:33,236 --> 00:03:37,011
Two years later, Project Wildfire would almost

75
00:03:37,011 --> 00:03:38,817
quadruple that number.

76
00:03:39,267 --> 00:03:41,400
Late winter, 2015.

77
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:46,551
Project Wildfire ran from February 23 to March 31.

78
00:03:46,551 --> 00:03:50,593
The HSI National Gang Unit led it, with 215

79
00:03:50,593 --> 00:03:52,943
law enforcement partners.

80
00:03:53,393 --> 00:03:56,389
In Fort Worth, Texas, the teams kept working

81
00:03:56,389 --> 00:03:57,139
after dark.

82
00:03:57,139 --> 00:03:58,296
Cars pulled over.

83
00:03:58,296 --> 00:04:00,135
Tattoos checked. Handcuffs.

84
00:04:00,585 --> 00:04:03,296
In Arlington, Virginia, a team went up the

85
00:04:03,296 --> 00:04:05,555
front steps of a building at night.

86
00:04:06,005 --> 00:04:08,700
In the Detroit area, sheriff's deputies and

87
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:11,019
agents walked a man to a waiting car.

88
00:04:11,469 --> 00:04:14,811
ICE said the busiest areas were San Juan,

89
00:04:14,811 --> 00:04:18,234
Puerto Rico. Dallas. El Paso. Los Angeles.

90
00:04:18,234 --> 00:04:19,213
And Detroit.

91
00:04:19,663 --> 00:04:22,765
In Lubbock, Texas, alone, 122 known or

92
00:04:22,765 --> 00:04:27,010
suspected gang members and associates were arrested.

93
00:04:27,010 --> 00:04:28,887
Bloods. Crips. Sureños.

94
00:04:28,887 --> 00:04:30,357
The Mexican Mafia.

95
00:04:30,357 --> 00:04:31,989
The Texas Syndicate.

96
00:04:31,989 --> 00:04:33,785
The Aryan Brotherhood.

97
00:04:34,235 --> 00:04:37,635
In Puerto Rico and central Florida, 46 members

98
00:04:37,635 --> 00:04:40,961
of one criminal organization were arrested on

99
00:04:40,961 --> 00:04:44,582
charges including narcotics and money laundering.

100
00:04:45,032 --> 00:04:47,444
The Detroit area: 89 arrests.

101
00:04:47,444 --> 00:04:49,191
The Chicago area: 30.

102
00:04:49,191 --> 00:04:52,435
The Imperial Valley, in California: 28.

103
00:04:52,885 --> 00:04:54,783
So who was actually arrested?

104
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:58,952
In total, Wildfire made 1,207 arrests.

105
00:04:58,952 --> 00:05:02,573
976 were gang members and associates.

106
00:05:02,573 --> 00:05:06,976
The other 231 were arrested on other criminal

107
00:05:06,976 --> 00:05:10,401
charges, or immigration violations.

108
00:05:10,851 --> 00:05:15,106
Of the 976, 913 faced criminal charges.

109
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:20,451
63 were arrested on immigration violations alone.

110
00:05:20,901 --> 00:05:24,737
ICE said 650 had violent criminal histories.

111
00:05:24,737 --> 00:05:27,352
19 had active murder warrants.

112
00:05:27,352 --> 00:05:31,013
15 were wanted for rape or sexual assault.

113
00:05:31,463 --> 00:05:34,746
This was an immigration agency's operation.

114
00:05:34,746 --> 00:05:38,640
But most of the people arrested were U.S. citizens.

115
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:42,151
199 were foreign nationals, from 18 countries.

116
00:05:42,601 --> 00:05:46,117
Of those foreign nationals, 151 were gang

117
00:05:46,117 --> 00:05:48,003
members or associates.

118
00:05:48,003 --> 00:05:51,519
And of everyone arrested, 150 were women.

119
00:05:51,969 --> 00:05:55,146
Most were tied to the Sureños, the Norteños,

120
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:58,107
the Bloods, the Crips, Puerto Rican-based

121
00:05:58,107 --> 00:05:59,841
gangs, and prison gangs.

122
00:06:00,291 --> 00:06:02,668
Agents seized 82 firearms.

123
00:06:02,668 --> 00:06:06,966
Methamphetamine, cocaine, heroin and marijuana.

124
00:06:06,966 --> 00:06:08,521
$379,399 in cash.

125
00:06:08,521 --> 00:06:12,545
And counterfeit goods worth more than half a

126
00:06:12,545 --> 00:06:14,008
million dollars.

127
00:06:14,458 --> 00:06:18,062
ICE's director at the time, Sarah Saldaña, put

128
00:06:18,062 --> 00:06:19,002
it this way.

129
00:06:20,002 --> 00:06:22,742
Groups like these, she said, can spread like a

130
00:06:22,742 --> 00:06:23,159
cancer.

131
00:06:23,609 --> 00:06:26,671
And an HSI official, Mike Prado, said the goal

132
00:06:26,671 --> 00:06:29,333
was to keep gang members on their heels,

133
00:06:29,333 --> 00:06:31,929
constantly looking over their shoulder.

134
00:06:32,379 --> 00:06:34,918
He called Wildfire one of the largest

135
00:06:34,918 --> 00:06:38,005
operations the agency had ever conducted, and

136
00:06:38,005 --> 00:06:39,377
the most successful.

137
00:06:40,377 --> 00:06:43,039
Not everyone thought sweeps were enough.

138
00:06:43,039 --> 00:06:45,835
The Christian Science Monitor pointed to a

139
00:06:45,835 --> 00:06:48,830
federal estimate of more than 30,000 gangs in

140
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:51,758
the U S, and to experts who see big busts as

141
00:06:51,758 --> 00:06:54,754
short-term fixes, unless more is done to stop

142
00:06:54,754 --> 00:06:57,017
gangs from recruiting new members.

143
00:06:57,467 --> 00:07:00,431
And one thing the announcements did not include:

144
00:07:00,431 --> 00:07:03,333
how many of these arrests ended in convictions.

145
00:07:03,783 --> 00:07:05,789
Two years later, the record fell.

146
00:07:06,239 --> 00:07:10,530
From March 26 to May 6, 2017, HSI ran what it

147
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:14,153
called its largest gang surge to date.

148
00:07:14,603 --> 00:07:17,767
In April, in Carrollton, Texas, agents

149
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:21,263
arrested a man ICE's video describes as an

150
00:07:21,263 --> 00:07:22,761
MS-13 gang member.

151
00:07:22,761 --> 00:07:26,507
ICE did not release his name, or the charges.

152
00:07:26,957 --> 00:07:31,107
In San Antonio, agents arrested a gang associate.

153
00:07:31,107 --> 00:07:34,749
Searches turned up cocaine, meth, heroin, 4

154
00:07:34,749 --> 00:07:38,136
handguns, and more than $48,000 in cash.

155
00:07:38,586 --> 00:07:42,426
By the end of the six weeks, the total was

156
00:07:42,426 --> 00:07:43,706
1,378 arrests.

157
00:07:44,156 --> 00:07:48,143
1,098 faced criminal charges, including 21

158
00:07:48,143 --> 00:07:50,326
murder-related charges.

159
00:07:50,326 --> 00:07:54,503
280 were arrested on immigration violations.

160
00:07:54,953 --> 00:07:58,353
10 of those arrested had crossed the border as

161
00:07:58,353 --> 00:07:59,905
unaccompanied minors.

162
00:07:59,905 --> 00:08:02,123
9 were confirmed gang members.

163
00:08:02,123 --> 00:08:03,379
8 of them, MS-13.

164
00:08:03,829 --> 00:08:10,006
ICE said 1,095 were confirmed gang members or

165
00:08:10,006 --> 00:08:16,869
affiliates. Bloods, 137. Sureños, 118. MS-13, 104.

166
00:08:16,869 --> 00:08:18,379
Crips, 104.

167
00:08:18,829 --> 00:08:20,795
What counted as confirmed?

168
00:08:20,795 --> 00:08:22,610
ICE listed its criteria.

169
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:24,199
Admitting membership.

170
00:08:24,199 --> 00:08:26,392
A conviction under gang laws.

171
00:08:26,392 --> 00:08:27,905
Identifying tattoos.

172
00:08:27,905 --> 00:08:31,309
Or being named a member by a reliable source.

173
00:08:31,759 --> 00:08:34,442
On Long Island, those kinds of labels would

174
00:08:34,442 --> 00:08:35,940
soon be tested in court.

175
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:41,175
Again, most were U.S. citizens. 933 of them.

176
00:08:41,175 --> 00:08:44,112
445 were foreign nationals.

177
00:08:44,112 --> 00:08:47,483
And agents seized 238 firearms.

178
00:08:47,933 --> 00:08:51,420
In Falls Church, Virginia, agents arrested 11

179
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:54,830
MS-13 members at a stash house they had been

180
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:58,627
watching over reports of alleged sex trafficking.

181
00:08:58,627 --> 00:09:02,191
10 were held on immigration violations, one on

182
00:09:02,191 --> 00:09:03,509
criminal charges.

183
00:09:03,509 --> 00:09:06,841
In San Diego, a task force arrested 23 gang

184
00:09:06,841 --> 00:09:10,483
members and associates, and seized 17 firearms.

185
00:09:10,933 --> 00:09:14,129
ICE's acting director, Thomas Homan, said the

186
00:09:14,129 --> 00:09:16,757
threat was not limited to big cities.

187
00:09:17,757 --> 00:09:20,679
And one region got an operation of its own.

188
00:09:21,129 --> 00:09:24,466
In May 2017, ICE and its partners launched

189
00:09:24,466 --> 00:09:26,849
Operation Matador. The target:

190
00:09:26,849 --> 00:09:30,344
MS-13 and other gangs on Long Island, in New

191
00:09:30,344 --> 00:09:33,204
York City, and in the Hudson Valley.

192
00:09:33,654 --> 00:09:38,754
On March 29, 2018, teams made 24 more arrests.

193
00:09:38,754 --> 00:09:42,081
That brought the total to 475.

194
00:09:42,531 --> 00:09:44,292
Nassau County: 210.

195
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,145
Suffolk County: 177.

196
00:09:46,145 --> 00:09:50,872
Then Queens, Spring Valley, the Bronx and Brooklyn.

197
00:09:51,322 --> 00:09:54,664
274 of the arrests were MS-13.

198
00:09:54,664 --> 00:09:57,561
227 were criminal arrests.

199
00:09:57,561 --> 00:10:03,354
248 were administrative, for immigration violations.

200
00:10:03,804 --> 00:10:07,311
ICE's deputy director, Thomas Homan, said that

201
00:10:07,311 --> 00:10:10,742
since the operation began, violent crime tied

202
00:10:10,742 --> 00:10:13,716
to MS-13 and other gangs had gone down.

203
00:10:13,716 --> 00:10:17,452
He credited ICE's partnerships with local police.

204
00:10:17,452 --> 00:10:20,807
ICE did not publish figures to back that up.

205
00:10:21,257 --> 00:10:24,697
According to PBS Frontline, about 60 of the

206
00:10:24,697 --> 00:10:27,977
more than 400 people arrested in the Long

207
00:10:27,977 --> 00:10:30,937
Island operation had come to the U.S.

208
00:10:30,937 --> 00:10:32,857
as unaccompanied minors.

209
00:10:32,857 --> 00:10:36,297
ICE's own count, in March 2018, was higher.

210
00:10:36,747 --> 00:10:39,986
In August 2017, the federal Office of Refugee

211
00:10:39,986 --> 00:10:42,434
Resettlement adopted a new policy.

212
00:10:42,434 --> 00:10:45,673
Minors suspected of gang ties would be placed

213
00:10:45,673 --> 00:10:48,552
in some of the most restrictive juvenile

214
00:10:48,552 --> 00:10:50,784
detention facilities available.

215
00:10:51,234 --> 00:10:53,648
But not every detention held up.

216
00:10:53,648 --> 00:10:56,967
In December 2017, NPR reported that at least

217
00:10:56,967 --> 00:11:00,135
32 immigrant teens on Long Island had been

218
00:11:00,135 --> 00:11:02,927
arrested for alleged gang membership.

219
00:11:02,927 --> 00:11:05,869
Judges had already released 14 of them.

220
00:11:06,319 --> 00:11:09,533
One of them, a 16-year-old, was held for five

221
00:11:09,533 --> 00:11:10,033
months.

222
00:11:10,033 --> 00:11:13,247
Police said he had written the numbers 503 in

223
00:11:13,247 --> 00:11:14,533
