233
00:11:41,486 --> 00:11:44,389
violated the detained minors' due process

234
00:11:44,389 --> 00:11:47,859
rights, and that they were entitled to a hearing.

235
00:11:48,309 --> 00:11:51,345
Suffolk County's police commissioner told News

236
00:11:51,345 --> 00:11:54,382
12 Long Island that the federal ruling changed

237
00:11:54,382 --> 00:11:57,353
nothing, and that his department stood by its

238
00:11:57,353 --> 00:11:58,079
detentions.

239
00:11:58,529 --> 00:12:01,507
“We stand by every single detention that we

240
00:12:01,507 --> 00:12:03,308
collaborated with ICE on.”

241
00:12:04,308 --> 00:12:05,039
2013:

242
00:12:05,039 --> 00:12:10,007
263 gang arrests. 2015: 976. 2017:

243
00:12:10,007 --> 00:12:16,291
1,095 confirmed gang members or affiliates.

244
00:12:16,291 --> 00:12:19,067
And on Long Island:

245
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:21,844
475 arrests in all.

246
00:12:22,294 --> 00:12:25,460
Every surge was announced with a number. Arrests.

247
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,753
Gangs. Cities. Guns.

248
00:12:27,203 --> 00:12:29,333
The number measures the operation.

249
00:12:29,333 --> 00:12:31,840
What it can't show is what happens next.

250
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:34,597
In criminal courts, in immigration hearings,

251
00:12:34,597 --> 00:12:37,229
and on the streets the teams leave behind.

252
00:12:37,679 --> 00:12:39,604
Case file 008. Closed.

253
00:12:39,604 --> 00:12:42,842
The next file is already on the desk.
